BT /F1 11 Tf 54.00 511.00 Td (to transgression of duty. But here again, without looking to duty, all) Tj ET
BT /F1 11 Tf 54.00 496.00 Td (men have already the strongest and most intimate inclination to) Tj ET
BT /F1 11 Tf 54.00 481.00 Td (happiness, because it is just in this idea that all inclinations are) Tj ET
BT /F1 11 Tf 54.00 466.00 Td (combined in one total. But the precept of happiness is often of such a) Tj ET
BT /F1 11 Tf 54.00 451.00 Td (sort that it greatly interferes with some inclinations, and yet a man) Tj ET
BT /F1 11 Tf 54.00 436.00 Td (cannot form any definite and certain conception of the sum of) Tj ET
BT /F1 11 Tf 54.00 421.00 Td (satisfaction of all of them which is called happiness. It is not then to) Tj ET
BT /F1 11 Tf 54.00 406.00 Td (be wondered at that a single inclination, definite both as to what it) Tj ET
BT /F1 11 Tf 54.00 391.00 Td (promises and as to the time within which it can be gratified, is often) Tj ET
BT /F1 11 Tf 54.00 376.00 Td (able to overcome such a fluctuating idea, and that a gouty patient, for) Tj ET
BT /F1 11 Tf 54.00 361.00 Td (instance, can choose to enjoy what he likes, and to suffer what he) Tj ET
BT /F1 11 Tf 54.00 346.00 Td (may, since, according to his calculation, on this occasion at least, he) Tj ET
BT /F1 11 Tf 54.00 331.00 Td (has not sacrificed the enjoyment of the present moment to a possibly) Tj ET
BT /F1 11 Tf 54.00 316.00 Td (mistaken expectation of a happiness which is supposed to be found in) Tj ET
BT /F1 11 Tf 54.00 301.00 Td (health. But even in this case, if the general desire for happiness did not) Tj ET
BT /F1 11 Tf 54.00 286.00 Td (influence his will, and supposing that in his particular case health was) Tj ET
BT /F1 11 Tf 54.00 271.00 Td (not a necessary element in this calculation, there yet remains in this, as) Tj ET
BT /F1 11 Tf 54.00 256.00 Td (in all other cases, this law, namely, that he should promote his) Tj ET
BT /F1 11 Tf 54.00 241.00 Td (happiness not from inclination but from duty, and by this would his) Tj ET
BT /F1 11 Tf 54.00 226.00 Td (conduct first acquire true moral worth.) Tj ET
BT /F1 11 Tf 68.00 207.00 Td (It is in this manner, undoubtedly, that we are to understand those) Tj ET
BT /F1 11 Tf 54.00 192.00 Td (passages of Scripture also in which we are commanded to love our) Tj ET
BT /F1 11 Tf 54.00 177.00 Td (neighbour, even our enemy. For love, as an affection, cannot be) Tj ET
BT /F1 11 Tf 54.00 162.00 Td (commanded, but beneficence for duty's sake may; even though we are) Tj ET
BT /F1 11 Tf 54.00 147.00 Td (not impelled to it by any inclination- nay, are even repelled by a) Tj ET
BT /F1 11 Tf 54.00 132.00 Td (natural and unconquerable aversion. This is practical love and not) Tj ET
BT /F1 11 Tf 54.00 117.00 Td (pathological- a love which is seated in the will, and not in the) Tj ET
BT /F1 11 Tf 54.00 102.00 Td (propensions of sense- in principles of action and not of tender) Tj ET
BT /F1 11 Tf 54.00 87.00 Td (sympathy; and it is this love alone which can be commanded.) Tj ET
