BT /F1 11 Tf 68.00 541.00 Td (The second proposition is: That an action done from duty derives its) Tj ET
BT /F1 11 Tf 54.00 526.00 Td (moral worth, not from the purpose which is to be attained by it, but) Tj ET
BT /F1 11 Tf 54.00 511.00 Td (from the maxim by which it is determined, and therefore does not) Tj ET
BT /F1 11 Tf 54.00 496.00 Td (depend on the realization of the object of the action, but merely on the) Tj ET
BT /F1 11 Tf 54.00 481.00 Td (principle of volition by which the action has taken place, without) Tj ET
BT /F1 11 Tf 54.00 466.00 Td (regard to any object of desire. It is clear from what precedes that the) Tj ET
BT /F1 11 Tf 54.00 451.00 Td (purposes which we may have in view in our actions, or their effects) Tj ET
BT /F1 11 Tf 54.00 436.00 Td (regarded as ends and springs of the will, cannot give to actions any) Tj ET
BT /F1 11 Tf 54.00 421.00 Td (unconditional or moral worth. In what, then, can their worth lie, if it is) Tj ET
BT /F1 11 Tf 54.00 406.00 Td (not to consist in the will and in reference to its expected effect? It) Tj ET
BT /F1 11 Tf 54.00 391.00 Td (cannot lie anywhere but in the principle of the will without regard to) Tj ET
BT /F1 11 Tf 54.00 376.00 Td (the ends which can be attained by the action. For the will stands) Tj ET
BT /F1 11 Tf 54.00 361.00 Td (between its a priori principle, which is formal, and its a posteriori) Tj ET
BT /F1 11 Tf 54.00 346.00 Td (spring, which is material, as between two roads, and as it must be) Tj ET
BT /F1 11 Tf 54.00 331.00 Td (determined by something, it follows that it must be determined by the) Tj ET
BT /F1 11 Tf 54.00 316.00 Td (formal principle of volition when an action is done from duty, in) Tj ET
BT /F1 11 Tf 54.00 301.00 Td (which case every material principle has been withdrawn from it.) Tj ET
BT /F1 11 Tf 68.00 282.00 Td (The third proposition, which is a consequence of the two preceding, I) Tj ET
BT /F1 11 Tf 54.00 267.00 Td (would express thus: Duty is the necessity of acting from respect for) Tj ET
BT /F1 11 Tf 54.00 252.00 Td (the law. I may have inclination for an object as the effect of my) Tj ET
BT /F1 11 Tf 54.00 237.00 Td (proposed action, but I cannot have respect for it, just for this reason,) Tj ET
BT /F1 11 Tf 54.00 222.00 Td (that it is an effect and not an energy of will. Similarly I cannot have) Tj ET
BT /F1 11 Tf 54.00 207.00 Td (respect for inclination, whether my own or another's; I can at most, if) Tj ET
BT /F1 11 Tf 54.00 192.00 Td (my own, approve it; if another's, sometimes even love it; i.e., look on) Tj ET
BT /F1 11 Tf 54.00 177.00 Td (it as favourable to my own interest. It is only what is connected with) Tj ET
BT /F1 11 Tf 54.00 162.00 Td (my will as a principle, by no means as an effect- what does not) Tj ET
BT /F1 11 Tf 54.00 147.00 Td (subserve my inclination, but overpowers it, or at least in case of) Tj ET
BT /F1 11 Tf 54.00 132.00 Td (choice excludes it from its calculation- in other words, simply the law) Tj ET
BT /F1 11 Tf 54.00 117.00 Td (of itself, which can be an object of respect, and hence a command.) Tj ET
BT /F1 11 Tf 54.00 102.00 Td (Now an action done from duty must wholly exclude the influence of) Tj ET
BT /F1 11 Tf 54.00 87.00 Td (inclination and with it every object of the will, so that nothing remains) Tj ET
BT /F1 11 Tf 54.00 72.00 Td (which can determine the will except objectively the law, and) Tj ET
BT /F1 9 Tf 205.50 28 Td (16) Tj ET
