BT /F1 11 Tf 54.00 541.00 Td (subjectively pure respect for this practical law, and consequently the) Tj ET
BT /F1 11 Tf 54.00 526.00 Td (maxim * that I should follow this law even to the thwarting of all my) Tj ET
BT /F1 11 Tf 54.00 511.00 Td (inclinations.) Tj ET
BT /F1 11 Tf 68.00 492.00 Td (* A maxim is the subjective principle of volition. The objective) Tj ET
BT /F1 11 Tf 54.00 477.00 Td (principle \(i.e., that which would also serve subjectively as a practical) Tj ET
BT /F1 11 Tf 54.00 462.00 Td (principle to all rational beings if reason had full power over the faculty) Tj ET
BT /F1 11 Tf 54.00 447.00 Td (of desire\) is the practical law.) Tj ET
BT /F1 11 Tf 68.00 428.00 Td (Thus the moral worth of an action does not lie in the effect expected) Tj ET
BT /F1 11 Tf 54.00 413.00 Td (from it, nor in any principle of action which requires to borrow its) Tj ET
BT /F1 11 Tf 54.00 398.00 Td (motive from this expected effect. For all these effects- agreeableness) Tj ET
BT /F1 11 Tf 54.00 383.00 Td (of one's condition and even the promotion of the happiness of others-) Tj ET
BT /F1 11 Tf 54.00 368.00 Td (could have been also brought about by other causes, so that for this) Tj ET
BT /F1 11 Tf 54.00 353.00 Td (there would have been no need of the will of a rational being; whereas) Tj ET
BT /F1 11 Tf 54.00 338.00 Td (it is in this alone that the supreme and unconditional good can be) Tj ET
BT /F1 11 Tf 54.00 323.00 Td (found. The pre-eminent good which we call moral can therefore) Tj ET
BT /F1 11 Tf 54.00 308.00 Td (consist in nothing else than the conception of law in itself, which) Tj ET
BT /F1 11 Tf 54.00 293.00 Td (certainly is only possible in a rational being, in so far as this) Tj ET
BT /F1 11 Tf 54.00 278.00 Td (conception, and not the expected effect, determines the will. This is a) Tj ET
BT /F1 11 Tf 54.00 263.00 Td (good which is already present in the person who acts accordingly, and) Tj ET
