BT /F1 11 Tf 54.00 316.00 Td (philosophy this may be permitted, or may even at times be necessary;) Tj ET
BT /F1 11 Tf 54.00 301.00 Td (but since moral laws ought to hold good for every rational creature,) Tj ET
BT /F1 11 Tf 54.00 286.00 Td (we must derive them from the general concept of a rational being. In) Tj ET
BT /F1 11 Tf 54.00 271.00 Td (this way, although for its application to man morality has need of) Tj ET
BT /F1 11 Tf 54.00 256.00 Td (anthropology, yet, in the first instance, we must treat it independently) Tj ET
