BT /F1 11 Tf 54.00 541.00 Td (categorical imperative which declares an action to be objectively) Tj ET
BT /F1 11 Tf 54.00 526.00 Td (necessary in itself without reference to any purpose, i.e., without any) Tj ET
BT /F1 11 Tf 54.00 511.00 Td (other end, is valid as an apodeictic \(practical\) principle.) Tj ET
BT /F1 11 Tf 68.00 492.00 Td (Whatever is possible only by the power of some rational being may) Tj ET
BT /F1 11 Tf 54.00 477.00 Td (also be conceived as a possible purpose of some will; and therefore) Tj ET
BT /F1 11 Tf 54.00 462.00 Td (the principles of action as regards the means necessary to attain some) Tj ET
BT /F1 11 Tf 54.00 447.00 Td (possible purpose are in fact infinitely numerous. All sciences have a) Tj ET
BT /F1 11 Tf 54.00 432.00 Td (practical part, consisting of problems expressing that some end is) Tj ET
BT /F1 11 Tf 54.00 417.00 Td (possible for us and of imperatives directing how it may be attained.) Tj ET
BT /F1 11 Tf 54.00 402.00 Td (These may, therefore, be called in general imperatives of skill. Here) Tj ET
BT /F1 11 Tf 54.00 387.00 Td (there is no question whether the end is rational and good, but only) Tj ET
BT /F1 11 Tf 54.00 372.00 Td (what one must do in order to attain it. The precepts for the physician) Tj ET
BT /F1 11 Tf 54.00 357.00 Td (to make his patient thoroughly healthy, and for a poisoner to ensure) Tj ET
BT /F1 11 Tf 54.00 342.00 Td (certain death, are of equal value in this respect, that each serves to) Tj ET
BT /F1 11 Tf 54.00 327.00 Td (effect its purpose perfectly. Since in early youth it cannot be known) Tj ET
BT /F1 11 Tf 54.00 312.00 Td (what ends are likely to occur to us in the course of life, parents seek to) Tj ET
BT /F1 11 Tf 54.00 297.00 Td (have their children taught a great many things, and provide for their) Tj ET
BT /F1 11 Tf 54.00 282.00 Td (skill in the use of means for all sorts of arbitrary ends, of none of) Tj ET
BT /F1 11 Tf 54.00 267.00 Td (which can they determine whether it may not perhaps hereafter be an) Tj ET
BT /F1 11 Tf 54.00 252.00 Td (object to their pupil, but which it is at all events possible that he might) Tj ET
BT /F1 11 Tf 54.00 237.00 Td (aim at; and this anxiety is so great that they commonly neglect to form) Tj ET
BT /F1 11 Tf 54.00 222.00 Td (and correct their judgement on the value of the things which may be) Tj ET
BT /F1 11 Tf 54.00 207.00 Td (chosen as ends.) Tj ET
BT /F1 11 Tf 68.00 188.00 Td (There is one end, however, which may be assumed to be actually such) Tj ET
BT /F1 11 Tf 54.00 173.00 Td (to all rational beings \(so far as imperatives apply to them, viz., as) Tj ET
BT /F1 11 Tf 54.00 158.00 Td (dependent beings\), and, therefore, one purpose which they not merely) Tj ET
BT /F1 11 Tf 54.00 143.00 Td (may have, but which we may with certainty assume that they all) Tj ET
BT /F1 11 Tf 54.00 128.00 Td (actually have by a natural necessity, and this is happiness. The) Tj ET
BT /F1 11 Tf 54.00 113.00 Td (hypothetical imperative which expresses the practical necessity of an) Tj ET
BT /F1 11 Tf 54.00 98.00 Td (action as means to the advancement of happiness is assertorial. We are) Tj ET
BT /F1 11 Tf 54.00 83.00 Td (not to present it as necessary for an uncertain and merely possible) Tj ET
BT /F1 9 Tf 205.50 28 Td (33) Tj ET
