BT /F1 11 Tf 68.00 507.00 Td (The will is conceived as a faculty of determining oneself to action in) Tj ET
BT /F1 11 Tf 54.00 492.00 Td (accordance with the conception of certain laws. And such a faculty) Tj ET
BT /F1 11 Tf 54.00 477.00 Td (can be found only in rational beings. Now that which serves the will) Tj ET
BT /F1 11 Tf 54.00 462.00 Td (as the objective ground of its self-determination is the end, and, if this) Tj ET
BT /F1 11 Tf 54.00 447.00 Td (is assigned by reason alone, it must hold for all rational beings. On the) Tj ET
BT /F1 11 Tf 54.00 432.00 Td (other hand, that which merely contains the ground of possibility of the) Tj ET
BT /F1 11 Tf 54.00 417.00 Td (action of which the effect is the end, this is called the means. The) Tj ET
BT /F1 11 Tf 54.00 402.00 Td (subjective ground of the desire is the spring, the objective ground of) Tj ET
BT /F1 11 Tf 54.00 387.00 Td (the volition is the motive; hence the distinction between subjective) Tj ET
BT /F1 11 Tf 54.00 372.00 Td (ends which rest on springs, and objective ends which depend on) Tj ET
BT /F1 11 Tf 54.00 357.00 Td (motives valid for every rational being. Practical principles are formal) Tj ET
BT /F1 11 Tf 54.00 342.00 Td (when they abstract from all subjective ends; they are material when) Tj ET
BT /F1 11 Tf 54.00 327.00 Td (they assume these, and therefore particular springs of action. The ends) Tj ET
BT /F1 11 Tf 54.00 312.00 Td (which a rational being proposes to himself at pleasure as effects of his) Tj ET
BT /F1 11 Tf 54.00 297.00 Td (actions \(material ends\) are all only relative, for it is only their relation) Tj ET
BT /F1 11 Tf 54.00 282.00 Td (to the particular desires of the subject that gives them their worth,) Tj ET
BT /F1 11 Tf 54.00 267.00 Td (which therefore cannot furnish principles universal and necessary for) Tj ET
BT /F1 11 Tf 54.00 252.00 Td (all rational beings and for every volition, that is to say practical laws.) Tj ET
BT /F1 11 Tf 54.00 237.00 Td (Hence all these relative ends can give rise only to hypothetical) Tj ET
BT /F1 11 Tf 54.00 222.00 Td (imperatives.) Tj ET
BT /F1 11 Tf 68.00 203.00 Td (Supposing, however, that there were something whose existence has) Tj ET
BT /F1 11 Tf 54.00 188.00 Td (in itself an absolute worth, something which, being an end in itself,) Tj ET
BT /F1 11 Tf 54.00 173.00 Td (could be a source of definite laws; then in this and this alone would lie) Tj ET
BT /F1 11 Tf 54.00 158.00 Td (the source of a possible categorical imperative, i.e., a practical law.) Tj ET
BT /F1 11 Tf 68.00 139.00 Td (Now I say: man and generally any rational being exists as an end in) Tj ET
BT /F1 11 Tf 54.00 124.00 Td (himself, not merely as a means to be arbitrarily used by this or that) Tj ET
BT /F1 11 Tf 54.00 109.00 Td (will, but in all his actions, whether they concern himself or other) Tj ET
BT /F1 11 Tf 54.00 94.00 Td (rational beings, must be always regarded at the same time as an end.) Tj ET
