BT /F1 11 Tf 54.00 286.00 Td (would possess absolute worth; but if all worth were conditioned and) Tj ET
BT /F1 11 Tf 54.00 271.00 Td (therefore contingent, then there would be no supreme practical) Tj ET
BT /F1 11 Tf 54.00 256.00 Td (principle of reason whatever.) Tj ET
BT /F1 11 Tf 68.00 237.00 Td (If then there is a supreme practical principle or, in respect of the) Tj ET
BT /F1 11 Tf 54.00 222.00 Td (human will, a categorical imperative, it must be one which, being) Tj ET
BT /F1 11 Tf 54.00 207.00 Td (drawn from the conception of that which is necessarily an end for) Tj ET
BT /F1 11 Tf 54.00 192.00 Td (everyone because it is an end in itself, constitutes an objective) Tj ET
BT /F1 11 Tf 54.00 177.00 Td (principle of will, and can therefore serve as a universal practical law.) Tj ET
BT /F1 11 Tf 54.00 162.00 Td (The foundation of this principle is: rational nature exists as an end in) Tj ET
BT /F1 11 Tf 54.00 147.00 Td (itself. Man necessarily conceives his own existence as being so; so far) Tj ET
BT /F1 11 Tf 54.00 132.00 Td (then this is a subjective principle of human actions. But every other) Tj ET
BT /F1 11 Tf 54.00 117.00 Td (rational being regards its existence similarly, just on the same rational) Tj ET
BT /F1 11 Tf 54.00 102.00 Td (principle that holds for me: * so that it is at the same time an objective) Tj ET
BT /F1 11 Tf 54.00 87.00 Td (principle, from which as a supreme practical law all laws of the will) Tj ET
BT /F1 11 Tf 54.00 72.00 Td (must be capable of being deduced. Accordingly the practical) Tj ET
