BT /F1 11 Tf 54.00 541.00 Td (imperative will be as follows: So act as to treat humanity, whether in) Tj ET
BT /F1 11 Tf 54.00 526.00 Td (thine own person or in that of any other, in every case as an end) Tj ET
BT /F1 11 Tf 54.00 511.00 Td (withal, never as means only. We will now inquire whether this can be) Tj ET
BT /F1 11 Tf 54.00 496.00 Td (practically carried out.) Tj ET
BT /F1 11 Tf 68.00 477.00 Td (* This proposition is here stated as a postulate. The ground of it will) Tj ET
BT /F1 11 Tf 54.00 462.00 Td (be found in the concluding section.) Tj ET
BT /F1 11 Tf 68.00 443.00 Td (To abide by the previous examples:) Tj ET
BT /F1 11 Tf 68.00 424.00 Td (Firstly, under the head of necessary duty to oneself: He who) Tj ET
BT /F1 11 Tf 54.00 409.00 Td (contemplates suicide should ask himself whether his action can be) Tj ET
BT /F1 11 Tf 54.00 394.00 Td (consistent with the idea of humanity as an end in itself. If he destroys) Tj ET
BT /F1 11 Tf 54.00 379.00 Td (himself in order to escape from painful circumstances, he uses a) Tj ET
BT /F1 11 Tf 54.00 364.00 Td (person merely as a mean to maintain a tolerable condition up to the) Tj ET
BT /F1 11 Tf 54.00 349.00 Td (end of life. But a man is not a thing, that is to say, something which) Tj ET
BT /F1 11 Tf 54.00 334.00 Td (can be used merely as means, but must in all his actions be always) Tj ET
BT /F1 11 Tf 54.00 319.00 Td (considered as an end in himself. I cannot, therefore, dispose in any) Tj ET
BT /F1 11 Tf 54.00 304.00 Td (way of a man in my own person so as to mutilate him, to damage or) Tj ET
BT /F1 11 Tf 54.00 289.00 Td (kill him. \(It belongs to ethics proper to define this principle more) Tj ET
BT /F1 11 Tf 54.00 274.00 Td (precisely, so as to avoid all misunderstanding, e. g., as to the) Tj ET
BT /F1 11 Tf 54.00 259.00 Td (amputation of the limbs in order to preserve myself, as to exposing my) Tj ET
BT /F1 11 Tf 54.00 244.00 Td (life to danger with a view to preserve it, etc. This question is therefore) Tj ET
BT /F1 11 Tf 54.00 229.00 Td (omitted here.\)) Tj ET
BT /F1 11 Tf 68.00 210.00 Td (Secondly, as regards necessary duties, or those of strict obligation,) Tj ET
BT /F1 11 Tf 54.00 195.00 Td (towards others: He who is thinking of making a lying promise to) Tj ET
BT /F1 11 Tf 54.00 180.00 Td (others will see at once that he would be using another man merely as a) Tj ET
BT /F1 11 Tf 54.00 165.00 Td (mean, without the latter containing at the same time the end in) Tj ET
BT /F1 11 Tf 54.00 150.00 Td (himself. For he whom I propose by such a promise to use for my own) Tj ET
BT /F1 11 Tf 54.00 135.00 Td (purposes cannot possibly assent to my mode of acting towards him) Tj ET
BT /F1 11 Tf 54.00 120.00 Td (and, therefore, cannot himself contain the end of this action. This) Tj ET
BT /F1 11 Tf 54.00 105.00 Td (violation of the principle of humanity in other men is more obvious if) Tj ET
BT /F1 11 Tf 54.00 90.00 Td (we take in examples of attacks on the freedom and property of others.) Tj ET
BT /F1 11 Tf 54.00 75.00 Td (For then it is clear that he who transgresses the rights of men intends) Tj ET
BT /F1 9 Tf 205.50 28 Td (49) Tj ET
