BT /F1 11 Tf 68.00 541.00 Td (This principle, that humanity and generally every rational nature is an) Tj ET
BT /F1 11 Tf 54.00 526.00 Td (end in itself \(which is the supreme limiting condition of every man's) Tj ET
BT /F1 11 Tf 54.00 511.00 Td (freedom of action\), is not borrowed from experience, firstly, because it) Tj ET
BT /F1 11 Tf 54.00 496.00 Td (is universal, applying as it does to all rational beings whatever, and) Tj ET
BT /F1 11 Tf 54.00 481.00 Td (experience is not capable of determining anything about them;) Tj ET
BT /F1 11 Tf 54.00 466.00 Td (secondly, because it does not present humanity as an end to men) Tj ET
BT /F1 11 Tf 54.00 451.00 Td (\(subjectively\), that is as an object which men do of themselves) Tj ET
BT /F1 11 Tf 54.00 436.00 Td (actually adopt as an end; but as an objective end, which must as a law) Tj ET
BT /F1 11 Tf 54.00 421.00 Td (constitute the supreme limiting condition of all our subjective ends, let) Tj ET
BT /F1 11 Tf 54.00 406.00 Td (them be what we will; it must therefore spring from pure reason. In) Tj ET
BT /F1 11 Tf 54.00 391.00 Td (fact the objective principle of all practical legislation lies \(according to) Tj ET
BT /F1 11 Tf 54.00 376.00 Td (the first principle\) in the rule and its form of universality which makes) Tj ET
BT /F1 11 Tf 54.00 361.00 Td (it capable of being a law \(say, e. g., a law of nature\); but the subjective) Tj ET
BT /F1 11 Tf 54.00 346.00 Td (principle is in the end; now by the second principle the subject of all) Tj ET
BT /F1 11 Tf 54.00 331.00 Td (ends is each rational being, inasmuch as it is an end in itself. Hence) Tj ET
BT /F1 11 Tf 54.00 316.00 Td (follows the third practical principle of the will, which is the ultimate) Tj ET
BT /F1 11 Tf 54.00 301.00 Td (condition of its harmony with universal practical reason, viz.: the idea) Tj ET
BT /F1 11 Tf 54.00 286.00 Td (of the will of every rational being as a universally legislative will.) Tj ET
BT /F1 11 Tf 68.00 267.00 Td (On this principle all maxims are rejected which are inconsistent with) Tj ET
BT /F1 11 Tf 54.00 252.00 Td (the will being itself universal legislator. Thus the will is not subject) Tj ET
BT /F1 11 Tf 54.00 237.00 Td (simply to the law, but so subject that it must be regarded as itself) Tj ET
BT /F1 11 Tf 54.00 222.00 Td (giving the law and, on this ground only, subject to the law \(of which it) Tj ET
BT /F1 11 Tf 54.00 207.00 Td (can regard itself as the author\).) Tj ET
BT /F1 11 Tf 68.00 188.00 Td (In the previous imperatives, namely, that based on the conception of) Tj ET
BT /F1 11 Tf 54.00 173.00 Td (the conformity of actions to general laws, as in a physical system of) Tj ET
BT /F1 11 Tf 54.00 158.00 Td (nature, and that based on the universal prerogative of rational beings) Tj ET
BT /F1 11 Tf 54.00 143.00 Td (as ends in themselves- these imperatives, just because they were) Tj ET
BT /F1 11 Tf 54.00 128.00 Td (conceived as categorical, excluded from any share in their authority all) Tj ET
BT /F1 11 Tf 54.00 113.00 Td (admixture of any interest as a spring of action; they were, however,) Tj ET
BT /F1 11 Tf 54.00 98.00 Td (only assumed to be categorical, because such an assumption was) Tj ET
BT /F1 11 Tf 54.00 83.00 Td (necessary to explain the conception of duty. But we could not prove) Tj ET
BT /F1 9 Tf 205.50 28 Td (51) Tj ET
