BT /F1 11 Tf 54.00 541.00 Td (morality, we need not wonder why they all failed. It was seen that man) Tj ET
BT /F1 11 Tf 54.00 526.00 Td (was bound to laws by duty, but it was not observed that the laws to) Tj ET
BT /F1 11 Tf 54.00 511.00 Td (which he is subject are only those of his own giving, though at the) Tj ET
BT /F1 11 Tf 54.00 496.00 Td (same time they are universal, and that he is only bound to act in) Tj ET
BT /F1 11 Tf 54.00 481.00 Td (conformity with his own will; a will, however, which is designed by) Tj ET
BT /F1 11 Tf 54.00 466.00 Td (nature to give universal laws. For when one has conceived man only) Tj ET
BT /F1 11 Tf 54.00 451.00 Td (as subject to a law \(no matter what\), then this law required some) Tj ET
BT /F1 11 Tf 54.00 436.00 Td (interest, either by way of attraction or constraint, since it did not) Tj ET
BT /F1 11 Tf 54.00 421.00 Td (originate as a law from his own will, but this will was according to a) Tj ET
BT /F1 11 Tf 54.00 406.00 Td (law obliged by something else to act in a certain manner. Now by this) Tj ET
BT /F1 11 Tf 54.00 391.00 Td (necessary consequence all the labour spent in finding a supreme) Tj ET
BT /F1 11 Tf 54.00 376.00 Td (principle of duty was irrevocably lost. For men never elicited duty, but) Tj ET
BT /F1 11 Tf 54.00 361.00 Td (only a necessity of acting from a certain interest. Whether this interest) Tj ET
BT /F1 11 Tf 54.00 346.00 Td (was private or otherwise, in any case the imperative must be) Tj ET
BT /F1 11 Tf 54.00 331.00 Td (conditional and could not by any means be capable of being a moral) Tj ET
BT /F1 11 Tf 54.00 316.00 Td (command. I will therefore call this the principle of autonomy of the) Tj ET
BT /F1 11 Tf 54.00 301.00 Td (will, in contrast with every other which I accordingly reckon as) Tj ET
BT /F1 11 Tf 54.00 286.00 Td (heteronomy.) Tj ET
BT /F1 11 Tf 68.00 267.00 Td (The conception of the will of every rational being as one which must) Tj ET
BT /F1 11 Tf 54.00 252.00 Td (consider itself as giving in all the maxims of its will universal laws, so) Tj ET
BT /F1 11 Tf 54.00 237.00 Td (as to judge itself and its actions from this point of view- this) Tj ET
BT /F1 11 Tf 54.00 222.00 Td (conception leads to another which depends on it and is very fruitful,) Tj ET
BT /F1 11 Tf 54.00 207.00 Td (namely that of a kingdom of ends.) Tj ET
BT /F1 11 Tf 68.00 188.00 Td (By a kingdom I understand the union of different rational beings in a) Tj ET
BT /F1 11 Tf 54.00 173.00 Td (system by common laws. Now since it is by laws that ends are) Tj ET
BT /F1 11 Tf 54.00 158.00 Td (determined as regards their universal validity, hence, if we abstract) Tj ET
BT /F1 11 Tf 54.00 143.00 Td (from the personal differences of rational beings and likewise from all) Tj ET
BT /F1 11 Tf 54.00 128.00 Td (the content of their private ends, we shall be able to conceive all ends) Tj ET
BT /F1 11 Tf 54.00 113.00 Td (combined in a systematic whole \(including both rational beings as) Tj ET
BT /F1 11 Tf 54.00 98.00 Td (ends in themselves, and also the special ends which each may propose) Tj ET
BT /F1 11 Tf 54.00 83.00 Td (to himself\), that is to say, we can conceive a kingdom of ends, which) Tj ET
