BT /F1 11 Tf 54.00 541.00 Td (on the preceding principles is possible.) Tj ET
BT /F1 11 Tf 68.00 522.00 Td (For all rational beings come under the law that each of them must treat) Tj ET
BT /F1 11 Tf 54.00 507.00 Td (itself and all others never merely as means, but in every case at the) Tj ET
BT /F1 11 Tf 54.00 492.00 Td (same time as ends in themselves. Hence results a systematic union of) Tj ET
BT /F1 11 Tf 54.00 477.00 Td (rational being by common objective laws, i.e., a kingdom which may) Tj ET
BT /F1 11 Tf 54.00 462.00 Td (be called a kingdom of ends, since what these laws have in view is just) Tj ET
BT /F1 11 Tf 54.00 447.00 Td (the relation of these beings to one another as ends and means. It is) Tj ET
BT /F1 11 Tf 54.00 432.00 Td (certainly only an ideal.) Tj ET
BT /F1 11 Tf 68.00 413.00 Td (A rational being belongs as a member to the kingdom of ends when,) Tj ET
BT /F1 11 Tf 54.00 398.00 Td (although giving universal laws in it, he is also himself subject to these) Tj ET
BT /F1 11 Tf 54.00 383.00 Td (laws. He belongs to it as sovereign when, while giving laws, he is not) Tj ET
BT /F1 11 Tf 54.00 368.00 Td (subject to the will of any other.) Tj ET
BT /F1 11 Tf 68.00 349.00 Td (A rational being must always regard himself as giving laws either as) Tj ET
BT /F1 11 Tf 54.00 334.00 Td (member or as sovereign in a kingdom of ends which is rendered) Tj ET
BT /F1 11 Tf 54.00 319.00 Td (possible by the freedom of will. He cannot, however, maintain the) Tj ET
BT /F1 11 Tf 54.00 304.00 Td (latter position merely by the maxims of his will, but only in case he is) Tj ET
BT /F1 11 Tf 54.00 289.00 Td (a completely independent being without wants and with unrestricted) Tj ET
BT /F1 11 Tf 54.00 274.00 Td (power adequate to his will.) Tj ET
BT /F1 11 Tf 68.00 255.00 Td (Morality consists then in the reference of all action to the legislation) Tj ET
BT /F1 11 Tf 54.00 240.00 Td (which alone can render a kingdom of ends possible. This legislation) Tj ET
BT /F1 11 Tf 54.00 225.00 Td (must be capable of existing in every rational being and of emanating) Tj ET
BT /F1 11 Tf 54.00 210.00 Td (from his will, so that the principle of this will is never to act on any) Tj ET
BT /F1 11 Tf 54.00 195.00 Td (maxim which could not without contradiction be also a universal law) Tj ET
BT /F1 11 Tf 54.00 180.00 Td (and, accordingly, always so to act that the will could at the same time) Tj ET
BT /F1 11 Tf 54.00 165.00 Td (regard itself as giving in its maxims universal laws. If now the maxims) Tj ET
BT /F1 11 Tf 54.00 150.00 Td (of rational beings are not by their own nature coincident with this) Tj ET
BT /F1 11 Tf 54.00 135.00 Td (objective principle, then the necessity of acting on it is called practical) Tj ET
BT /F1 11 Tf 54.00 120.00 Td (necessitation, i.e., duty. Duty does not apply to the sovereign in the) Tj ET
BT /F1 11 Tf 54.00 105.00 Td (kingdom of ends, but it does to every member of it and to all in the) Tj ET
BT /F1 11 Tf 54.00 90.00 Td (same degree.) Tj ET
BT /F1 11 Tf 68.00 71.00 Td (The practical necessity of acting on this principle, i.e., duty, does not) Tj ET
