BT /F1 11 Tf 54.00 541.00 Td (rest at all on feelings, impulses, or inclinations, but solely on the) Tj ET
BT /F1 11 Tf 54.00 526.00 Td (relation of rational beings to one another, a relation in which the will) Tj ET
BT /F1 11 Tf 54.00 511.00 Td (of a rational being must always be regarded as legislative, since) Tj ET
BT /F1 11 Tf 54.00 496.00 Td (otherwise it could not be conceived as an end in itself. Reason then) Tj ET
BT /F1 11 Tf 54.00 481.00 Td (refers every maxim of the will, regarding it as legislating universally,) Tj ET
BT /F1 11 Tf 54.00 466.00 Td (to every other will and also to every action towards oneself; and this) Tj ET
