BT /F1 11 Tf 54.00 541.00 Td (all rational beings. For as morality serves as a law for us only because) Tj ET
BT /F1 11 Tf 54.00 526.00 Td (we are rational beings, it must also hold for all rational beings; and as) Tj ET
BT /F1 11 Tf 54.00 511.00 Td (it must be deduced simply from the property of freedom, it must be) Tj ET
BT /F1 11 Tf 54.00 496.00 Td (shown that freedom also is a property of all rational beings. It is not) Tj ET
BT /F1 11 Tf 54.00 481.00 Td (enough, then, to prove it from certain supposed experiences of human) Tj ET
BT /F1 11 Tf 54.00 466.00 Td (nature \(which indeed is quite impossible, and it can only be shown a) Tj ET
BT /F1 11 Tf 54.00 451.00 Td (priori\), but we must show that it belongs to the activity of all rational) Tj ET
BT /F1 11 Tf 54.00 436.00 Td (beings endowed with a will. Now I say every being that cannot act) Tj ET
BT /F1 11 Tf 54.00 421.00 Td (except under the idea of freedom is just for that reason in a practical) Tj ET
BT /F1 11 Tf 54.00 406.00 Td (point of view really free, that is to say, all laws which are inseparably) Tj ET
BT /F1 11 Tf 54.00 391.00 Td (connected with freedom have the same force for him as if his will had) Tj ET
BT /F1 11 Tf 54.00 376.00 Td (been shown to be free in itself by a proof theoretically conclusive. *) Tj ET
BT /F1 11 Tf 54.00 361.00 Td (Now I affirm that we must attribute to every rational being which has) Tj ET
BT /F1 11 Tf 54.00 346.00 Td (a will that it has also the idea of freedom and acts entirely under this) Tj ET
BT /F1 11 Tf 54.00 331.00 Td (idea. For in such a being we conceive a reason that is practical, that is,) Tj ET
BT /F1 11 Tf 54.00 316.00 Td (has causality in reference to its objects. Now we cannot possibly) Tj ET
BT /F1 11 Tf 54.00 301.00 Td (conceive a reason consciously receiving a bias from any other quarter) Tj ET
BT /F1 11 Tf 54.00 286.00 Td (with respect to its judgements, for then the subject would ascribe the) Tj ET
BT /F1 11 Tf 54.00 271.00 Td (determination of its judgement not to its own reason, but to an) Tj ET
BT /F1 11 Tf 54.00 256.00 Td (impulse. It must regard itself as the author of its principles) Tj ET
BT /F1 11 Tf 54.00 241.00 Td (independent of foreign influences. Consequently as practical reason or) Tj ET
BT /F1 11 Tf 54.00 226.00 Td (as the will of a rational being it must regard itself as free, that is to) Tj ET
BT /F1 11 Tf 54.00 211.00 Td (say, the will of such a being cannot be a will of its own except under) Tj ET
BT /F1 11 Tf 54.00 196.00 Td (the idea of freedom. This idea must therefore in a practical point of) Tj ET
BT /F1 11 Tf 54.00 181.00 Td (view be ascribed to every rational being.) Tj ET
BT /F1 11 Tf 68.00 162.00 Td (* I adopt this method of assuming freedom merely as an idea which) Tj ET
BT /F1 11 Tf 54.00 147.00 Td (rational beings suppose in their actions, in order to avoid the necessity) Tj ET
BT /F1 11 Tf 54.00 132.00 Td (of proving it in its theoretical aspect also. The former is sufficient for) Tj ET
BT /F1 11 Tf 54.00 117.00 Td (my purpose; for even though the speculative proof should not be made) Tj ET
BT /F1 11 Tf 54.00 102.00 Td (out, yet a being that cannot act except with the idea of freedom is) Tj ET
BT /F1 11 Tf 54.00 87.00 Td (bound by the same laws that would oblige a being who was actually) Tj ET
BT /F1 11 Tf 54.00 72.00 Td (free. Thus we can escape here from the onus which presses on the) Tj ET
