BT /F1 11 Tf 54.00 541.00 Td (effect that the law exercises on the will, the objective principle of) Tj ET
BT /F1 11 Tf 54.00 526.00 Td (which is furnished by reason alone.) Tj ET
BT /F1 11 Tf 68.00 507.00 Td (* Interest is that by which reason becomes practical, i.e., a cause) Tj ET
BT /F1 11 Tf 54.00 492.00 Td (determining the will. Hence we say of rational beings only that they) Tj ET
BT /F1 11 Tf 54.00 477.00 Td (take an interest in a thing; irrational beings only feel sensual appetites.) Tj ET
BT /F1 11 Tf 54.00 462.00 Td (Reason takes a direct interest in action then only when the universal) Tj ET
BT /F1 11 Tf 54.00 447.00 Td (validity of its maxims is alone sufficient to determine the will. Such an) Tj ET
BT /F1 11 Tf 54.00 432.00 Td (interest alone is pure. But if it can determine the will only by means of) Tj ET
BT /F1 11 Tf 54.00 417.00 Td (another object of desire or on the suggestion of a particular feeling of) Tj ET
BT /F1 11 Tf 54.00 402.00 Td (the subject, then reason takes only an indirect interest in the action,) Tj ET
BT /F1 11 Tf 54.00 387.00 Td (and, as reason by itself without experience cannot discover either) Tj ET
BT /F1 11 Tf 54.00 372.00 Td (objects of the will or a special feeling actuating it, this latter interest) Tj ET
BT /F1 11 Tf 54.00 357.00 Td (would only be empirical and not a pure rational interest. The logical) Tj ET
BT /F1 11 Tf 54.00 342.00 Td (interest of reason \(namely, to extend its insight\) is never direct, but) Tj ET
BT /F1 11 Tf 54.00 327.00 Td (presupposes purposes for which reason is employed.) Tj ET
BT /F1 11 Tf 68.00 308.00 Td (In order indeed that a rational being who is also affected through the) Tj ET
BT /F1 11 Tf 54.00 293.00 Td (senses should will what reason alone directs such beings that they) Tj ET
BT /F1 11 Tf 54.00 278.00 Td (ought to will, it is no doubt requisite that reason should have a power) Tj ET
BT /F1 11 Tf 54.00 263.00 Td (to infuse a feeling of pleasure or satisfaction in the fulfilment of duty,) Tj ET
BT /F1 11 Tf 54.00 248.00 Td (that is to say, that it should have a causality by which it determines the) Tj ET
BT /F1 11 Tf 54.00 233.00 Td (sensibility according to its own principles. But it is quite impossible to) Tj ET
BT /F1 11 Tf 54.00 218.00 Td (discern, i.e., to make it intelligible a priori, how a mere thought, which) Tj ET
BT /F1 11 Tf 54.00 203.00 Td (itself contains nothing sensible, can itself produce a sensation of) Tj ET
BT /F1 11 Tf 54.00 188.00 Td (pleasure or pain; for this is a particular kind of causality of which as of) Tj ET
BT /F1 11 Tf 54.00 173.00 Td (every other causality we can determine nothing whatever a priori; we) Tj ET
BT /F1 11 Tf 54.00 158.00 Td (must only consult experience about it. But as this cannot supply us) Tj ET
BT /F1 11 Tf 54.00 143.00 Td (with any relation of cause and effect except between two objects of) Tj ET
BT /F1 11 Tf 54.00 128.00 Td (experience, whereas in this case, although indeed the effect produced) Tj ET
BT /F1 11 Tf 54.00 113.00 Td (lies within experience, yet the cause is supposed to be pure reason) Tj ET
BT /F1 11 Tf 54.00 98.00 Td (acting through mere ideas which offer no object to experience, it) Tj ET
BT /F1 11 Tf 54.00 83.00 Td (follows that for us men it is quite impossible to explain how and why) Tj ET
BT /F1 9 Tf 205.50 28 Td (83) Tj ET
endstream
