BT /F1 11 Tf 54.00 541.00 Td (the universality of the maxim as a law, that is, morality, interests. This) Tj ET
BT /F1 11 Tf 54.00 526.00 Td (only is certain, that it is not because it interests us that it has validity) Tj ET
BT /F1 11 Tf 54.00 511.00 Td (for us \(for that would be heteronomy and dependence of practical) Tj ET
BT /F1 11 Tf 54.00 496.00 Td (reason on sensibility, namely, on a feeling as its principle, in which) Tj ET
BT /F1 11 Tf 54.00 481.00 Td (case it could never give moral laws\), but that it interests us because it) Tj ET
BT /F1 11 Tf 54.00 466.00 Td (is valid for us as men, inasmuch as it had its source in our will as) Tj ET
BT /F1 11 Tf 54.00 451.00 Td (intelligences, in other words, in our proper self, and what belongs to) Tj ET
BT /F1 11 Tf 54.00 436.00 Td (mere appearance is necessarily subordinated by reason to the nature of) Tj ET
BT /F1 11 Tf 54.00 421.00 Td (the thing in itself.) Tj ET
BT /F1 11 Tf 68.00 402.00 Td (The question then, "How a categorical imperative is possible," can be) Tj ET
BT /F1 11 Tf 54.00 387.00 Td (answered to this extent, that we can assign the only hypothesis on) Tj ET
BT /F1 11 Tf 54.00 372.00 Td (which it is possible, namely, the idea of freedom; and we can also) Tj ET
BT /F1 11 Tf 54.00 357.00 Td (discern the necessity of this hypothesis, and this is sufficient for the) Tj ET
BT /F1 11 Tf 54.00 342.00 Td (practical exercise of reason, that is, for the conviction of the validity) Tj ET
BT /F1 11 Tf 54.00 327.00 Td (of this imperative, and hence of the moral law; but how this) Tj ET
BT /F1 11 Tf 54.00 312.00 Td (hypothesis itself is possible can never be discerned by any human) Tj ET
BT /F1 11 Tf 54.00 297.00 Td (reason. On the hypothesis, however, that the will of an intelligence is) Tj ET
BT /F1 11 Tf 54.00 282.00 Td (free, its autonomy, as the essential formal condition of its) Tj ET
BT /F1 11 Tf 54.00 267.00 Td (determination, is a necessary consequence. Moreover, this freedom of) Tj ET
BT /F1 11 Tf 54.00 252.00 Td (will is not merely quite possible as a hypothesis \(not involving any) Tj ET
BT /F1 11 Tf 54.00 237.00 Td (contradiction to the principle of physical necessity in the connexion of) Tj ET
BT /F1 11 Tf 54.00 222.00 Td (the phenomena of the sensible world\) as speculative philosophy can) Tj ET
BT /F1 11 Tf 54.00 207.00 Td (show: but further, a rational being who is conscious of causality) Tj ET
BT /F1 11 Tf 54.00 192.00 Td (through reason, that is to say, of a will \(distinct from desires\), must of) Tj ET
BT /F1 11 Tf 54.00 177.00 Td (necessity make it practically, that is, in idea, the condition of all his) Tj ET
BT /F1 11 Tf 54.00 162.00 Td (voluntary actions. But to explain how pure reason can be of itself) Tj ET
BT /F1 11 Tf 54.00 147.00 Td (practical without the aid of any spring of action that could be derived) Tj ET
BT /F1 11 Tf 54.00 132.00 Td (from any other source, i.e., how the mere principle of the universal) Tj ET
BT /F1 11 Tf 54.00 117.00 Td (validity of all its maxims as laws \(which would certainly be the form) Tj ET
BT /F1 11 Tf 54.00 102.00 Td (of a pure practical reason\) can of itself supply a spring, without any) Tj ET
BT /F1 11 Tf 54.00 87.00 Td (matter \(object\) of the will in which one could antecedently take any) Tj ET
BT /F1 11 Tf 54.00 72.00 Td (interest; and how it can produce an interest which would be called) Tj ET
BT /F1 9 Tf 205.50 28 Td (84) Tj ET
