BT /F1 11 Tf 54.00 541.00 Td (transcendent concepts which we call the intelligible world, and so lose) Tj ET
BT /F1 11 Tf 54.00 526.00 Td (itself amidst chimeras. For the rest, the idea of a pure world of) Tj ET
BT /F1 11 Tf 54.00 511.00 Td (understanding as a system of all intelligences, and to which we) Tj ET
BT /F1 11 Tf 54.00 496.00 Td (ourselves as rational beings belong \(although we are likewise on the) Tj ET
BT /F1 11 Tf 54.00 481.00 Td (other side members of the sensible world\), this remains always a) Tj ET
BT /F1 11 Tf 54.00 466.00 Td (useful and legitimate idea for the purposes of rational belief, although) Tj ET
BT /F1 11 Tf 54.00 451.00 Td (all knowledge stops at its threshold, useful, namely, to produce in us a) Tj ET
BT /F1 11 Tf 54.00 436.00 Td (lively interest in the moral law by means of the noble ideal of a) Tj ET
BT /F1 11 Tf 54.00 421.00 Td (universal kingdom of ends in themselves \(rational beings\), to which) Tj ET
BT /F1 11 Tf 54.00 406.00 Td (we can belong as members then only when we carefully conduct) Tj ET
BT /F1 11 Tf 54.00 391.00 Td (ourselves according to the maxims of freedom as if they were laws of) Tj ET
BT /F1 11 Tf 54.00 376.00 Td (nature.) Tj ET
BT /F1 11 Tf 68.00 357.00 Td (Concluding Remark) Tj ET
BT /F1 11 Tf 68.00 338.00 Td (The speculative employment of reason with respect to nature leads to) Tj ET
BT /F1 11 Tf 54.00 323.00 Td (the absolute necessity of some supreme cause of the world: the) Tj ET
BT /F1 11 Tf 54.00 308.00 Td (practical employment of reason with a view to freedom leads also to) Tj ET
BT /F1 11 Tf 54.00 293.00 Td (absolute necessity, but only of the laws of the actions of a rational) Tj ET
BT /F1 11 Tf 54.00 278.00 Td (being as such. Now it is an essential principle of reason, however) Tj ET
BT /F1 11 Tf 54.00 263.00 Td (employed, to push its knowledge to a consciousness of its necessity) Tj ET
BT /F1 11 Tf 54.00 248.00 Td (\(without which it would not be rational knowledge\). It is, however, an) Tj ET
BT /F1 11 Tf 54.00 233.00 Td (equally essential restriction of the same reason that it can neither) Tj ET
BT /F1 11 Tf 54.00 218.00 Td (discern the necessity of what is or what happens, nor of what ought to) Tj ET
BT /F1 11 Tf 54.00 203.00 Td (happen, unless a condition is supposed on which it is or happens or) Tj ET
BT /F1 11 Tf 54.00 188.00 Td (ought to happen. In this way, however, by the constant inquiry for the) Tj ET
BT /F1 11 Tf 54.00 173.00 Td (condition, the satisfaction of reason is only further and further) Tj ET
BT /F1 11 Tf 54.00 158.00 Td (postponed. Hence it unceasingly seeks the unconditionally necessary) Tj ET
BT /F1 11 Tf 54.00 143.00 Td (and finds itself forced to assume it, although without any means of) Tj ET
BT /F1 11 Tf 54.00 128.00 Td (making it comprehensible to itself, happy enough if only it can) Tj ET
BT /F1 11 Tf 54.00 113.00 Td (discover a conception which agrees with this assumption. It is) Tj ET
BT /F1 11 Tf 54.00 98.00 Td (therefore no fault in our deduction of the supreme principle of) Tj ET
BT /F1 11 Tf 54.00 83.00 Td (morality, but an objection that should be made to human reason in) Tj ET
